						"load",
						"transmit"
					]
				},
				"description": "By sending a load to a specified recipient, DUKE.ai processes the load by extracting data, classifying documents, as well as generating a DUKE Verified Score which is a conglomeration of correlation metrics and other variables about the load.\n\nTransmit as many loads as you like at once to a specified recipient, but be aware that these loads will end up being processed onto the same Schedule (if you have Schedule generation enabled for your pipeline).\n\nAlthough the \"recipient\" value is a list, when transmitting loads to a factoring endpoint or other integration email handle, only one recipient can be referenced. This helps keep invoice generation and other things in order when processing your load(s).\n\nTransmitting loads notifies the user referenced in the URI by email that their loads are being processed. To avoid this, pass a key (\"suppress_notifications\") with a string value of \"true\".\n\nAuthorization should be the id_token received when authenticating, and passed in the headers under the \"Authorization\" key."
			},
